    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e (safety net cli.py ~13940-13977). Live: `survey fx --out <symlink to /dev/full>` -> rc=1, 'internal error: OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device / This is a bug'; `survey --out <chmod 555 dir>/x.json` -> rc=1, 'internal error: PermissionError: [Errno 13]... This is a bug'. New facet: `sketch fx > /dev/full` prints the same two lines, then 'Exception ignored in: <_io.TextIOWrapper name=<stdout>> OSError: [Errno 28]' and exits rc=120. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nThe CLI's top-level safety net (cli.py main(), WI-himas, `except Exception as exc`) prints any uncaught OSError, including a full disk, as\n\n  hypergumbo: internal error: OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device\n  This is a bug; re-run with --debug for a full traceback.\n\nand returns 1. LIVE (dev 62602239c6): `python -m hypergumbo_core verify-claims ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/flask-restful --claims docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml --json > /dev/full` -> rc=1 with exactly those two lines. The same happens for `survey --out <symlink to /dev/full>`.\n\nA full disk (ENOSPC) or an exceeded quota (EDQUOT) is an ENVIRONMENT condition, not a hypergumbo bug. Telling the reader it is a bug sends them to diagnose code, which is the misdiagnosis WI-kovoj recorded (check-package-coverage exit 1 read as a coverage gap when /tmp was full). Expected: a typed message naming the condition and the path where it is known (e.g. \"hypergumbo: disk full writing <path> (ENOSPC); free space and re-run\"), a distinct non-zero exit, and no \"This is a bug\" line.\n\nSibling conditions to check before fixing (not checked): EACCES / EROFS on --out (observed: survey --out /dev/full -> \"internal error: PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/dev/full.slices'\", also labelled a bug), EPIPE (already handled separately just above the safety net).\n\nInstruments are already covered: scripts/lib/cohort_ledger.py (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kovoj) tees stderr and flags this text as DISK FULL in the cohort claim. This item is about the user-facing CLI."  # 96f1
